{
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "a01",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 2,
      "estimated_minutes": 2,
      "reason": "The description identifies the same three catch-alls discussed in d01 and directly raises whether the enumeration is exhaustive. The added ejusdem generis theory requires no independent resolution to check what problem the description names."
    },
    {
      "id": "a02",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 3,
      "estimated_minutes": 3,
      "reason": "One additional look at the letter's excluded 'Other Causes of Action' establishes the asserted relationship between the two paragraphs. The reviewer can then distinguish the category-overlap complaint from d01's treatment of the open-ended catch-alls without deciding whether the alleged overlap actually exists."
    },
    {
      "id": "a03",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 1,
      "estimated_minutes": 1,
      "reason": "The description expressly targets the tolling endpoint and the mangled 'of until' conjunction, while d02 concerns which claims 'or otherwise related to' reaches. The comparison requires no factual or cross-document inquiry."
    },
    {
      "id": "a04",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 2,
      "estimated_minutes": 2,
      "reason": "The April 28/April 30 discrepancy is immediately checkable against the incorporation clause and the letter's date. Checking the call does not require resolving document identity because the description expressly presents a misidentification problem rather than the breadth of 'not be limited to' addressed in d03."
    },
    {
      "id": "a05",
      "difficulty": "intermediate",
      "score": 4,
      "estimated_minutes": 5,
      "reason": "The reviewer must check both documents to verify the two tolling endpoints and identify the asserted conflict following dismissal. Once those references are checked, the endpoint-priority question is readily distinguishable from d03's question about tolling claims outside the original suit."
    },
    {
      "id": "a06",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 3,
      "estimated_minutes": 3,
      "reason": "The reviewer needs one further look at the heading and the opinion's quotation of 'sole remedy,' particularly given the degraded contract text. The description's later-breach trigger and remedy-exclusivity questions can then be compared directly with d04's focus on which claims refiling permits."
    },
    {
      "id": "a07",
      "difficulty": "intermediate",
      "score": 4,
      "estimated_minutes": 6,
      "reason": "The reviewer must verify the enforcement language in section V and the payment obligation in section IV, then separate the description's enforcement-versus-refiling theory from the court's use of other provisions to determine permissible claims. Section V also appears in the parties' arguments, so checking what the court actually relied on takes more than a phrase-level comparison."
    }
  ]
}
